quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  6,1,"All praise belongs to Allah, Who created the heavens and the earth and made (manifold) darknesses and the light. Yet the disbelievers equate (others) to their Lord."
  6,2,"He is the One Who created you from clay and then determined a term (of your life). (The knowledge of) the specified time (for your death) is with Him, yet you continue to doubt."
  6,3,And He is Allah in the heavens and on the earth; He knows your secret (thoughts) and your open (words and acts). And He knows what you earn.
  6,4,"Whenever a sign came to them from among the signs of their Lord, they used to turn away from it."
  6,5,"They indeed denied the truth when it came to them, but soon, the news will come to them regarding what they have been mocking."
  6,6,"Have they not realised how many generations We have destroyed before them? We had established them in the land in a way that We have never established you. And We sent (from the sky) abundant rains upon them and made rivers flow beneath them. Then, We destroyed them for their sins and brought about another generation after them."
  6,7,"(Esteemed Prophet!) Even if We had revealed to you a Book written on parchment, and they had touched it with their own hands, the disbelievers would (still) have said: ‘This is nothing but clear magic.’"
  6,8,"And they would say: ‘Why has an angel not been (physically) sent down to (support) him?’ But had We sent down an angel, the matter would have certainly been decreed (at once), and they would have never been given respite."
